<article class="env-lemma" id="0ERP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ERP">Lemma <span data-tag="0ERP">82.26.6</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $X/B$ be good. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be a triple as in Definition <a href="/tag/0ER1" data-tag="0ER1">82.22.1</a>. Then the rule that to $f : X' \to X$ assigns $(i')^* : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X') \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - 1}(D')$ where $D' = D \times _ X X'$ is a bivariant class of degree $1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0ERA" data-tag="0ERA">82.23.2</a>, <a href="/tag/0ER5" data-tag="0ER5">82.22.5</a>, <a href="/tag/0ER6" data-tag="0ER6">82.22.6</a>, and <a href="/tag/0ERC" data-tag="0ERC">82.23.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>